Falsifies `socket_contract::ephemeral::tests::a_stack_started_after_another_reuses_none_of_its_ports`.

The defect: the cursor is seeded once from the counter, as an earlier version seeded it
(the riscv64 counter's 10 MHz), instead of following the boot clock. Each stack's start is then
a point unrelated to the last stack's ports, and some gap lands it on them.

Expected to fail: the test's `!first.contains(p)` assertion, naming the boot time, gap and reused port.

